body:
If anyone wants a workaround:
```cs
[ExportToolButton("Refresh Item(s)")]
public Callable RefreshButton => Callable.From(RefreshData);

public void RefreshData()
{
    ResourceLoader.Load<Foo<T>>(ResourcePath, cacheMode: ResourceLoader.CacheMode.ReplaceDeep);
}
```
Change `Foo<T>` to your wanted class, but this will refresh the inspector and update the cache for the chosen file. I'm not sure why the values of type `T` aren't loaded into the cache.

P.S. It's not perfect, and does require the button be on the file. So if you have `Foo` as a local value inside `Bar`, you'll need to add this to `Bar` to work.
